// ★ E.4 PREREQUISITE: the loop ban reads the ROW, not the keyword.
//
// Two front-end checks refused an unmeasured `while` in a `func` on the strength of
// `kind == DECL_FUNCTION`, with a message advising "use 'proc'". Once `proc` starts disappearing
// that advice names a keyword that is going away, and every migrated loop becomes an error.
// `effects diverge` stands them down, as it already stood down the sovereign engine's obligation.
//
// ★ AND THE ROW PROPAGATES, which is what makes it worth reading. `main` calls a diverging
// function, so `main` diverges too — declaring only `effects io` on it is [E130] ("it also has:
// diverge"). A caller cannot inherit an effect silently; that is the difference between a row and
// a comment.
extern proc libc_printf(fmt *u8, ...) i32
func loop_forever(n i32) i32 effects io, diverge {
    var i i32 = 0
    while i < n { libc_printf("x") }
    return i
}
func main() i32 effects io, diverge { return loop_forever(0) }
